assets/qpdf.worker.js
  dist/qpdf.js of @neslinesli93/qpdf-wasm 0.3.0, unchanged, under a first
  line that says so and above a message handler that is quillify's own. It is
  the script that loads assets/qpdf.wasm and runs it. That package declares
  the ISC license, names no holder and ships no license text. The script
  names no author and no license. It is the JavaScript that Emscripten writes
  beside a binary it compiles, and Emscripten's own code is under the MIT
  license and the University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License
  (licenses/emscripten-LICENSE). The script does not say which Emscripten
  wrote it. That package's Dockerfile, at its tag 0.3.0, names the image
  emscripten/emsdk:3.1.74, and the text is that version's.

assets/qpdf.wasm
  dist/qpdf.wasm of @neslinesli93/qpdf-wasm 0.3.0, unchanged. Its SHA-256 is
  abd933f4ccace4f732999381b21aec8b7e3726f18a5b167fafd57f88dd440876.
  That package declares the ISC license, names no holder and ships no license
  text. What is linked into the binary follows, by the binary's own strings
  where it says and by that package's Dockerfile, at its tag 0.3.0, where it
  does not.

  qpdf 12.2.0, Copyright (c) 2005-2021 Jay Berkenbilt and Copyright (c)
  2022-2025 Jay Berkenbilt and Manfred Holger, under the Apache License 2.0
  (licenses/qpdf-LICENSE). Its notice is licenses/qpdf-NOTICE. The binary
  has qpdf's native crypto provider and no other, so it runs the two
  implementations that notice names: the SHA-2 of sphlib 3.0, Copyright (c)
  2007-2011 Projet RNRT SAPHIR, under the MIT license, whose text is in the
  notice, and Philip J. Erdelsky's Rijndael, which is in the public domain.

  libjpeg-turbo 2.1.1, Copyright (C) 1991-2021 The libjpeg-turbo Project and
  many others, from ImageMagick's copy of its source, under the licenses of
  licenses/libjpeg-turbo-LICENSE and of licenses/libjpeg-turbo-README.ijg,
  which the first names. This software is based in part on the work of the
  Independent JPEG Group.

  zlib, (C) 1995-2022 Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler, under the zlib
  license, which is the copyright notice in licenses/zlib-README. The binary
  carries zlib's messages and no version of it. The Dockerfile names the
  commit that is zlib 1.2.12, and the file is that version's.

  The runtime Emscripten links: its own code (licenses/emscripten-LICENSE),
  musl, under the MIT license (licenses/musl-COPYRIGHT), and LLVM's libc++,
  libc++abi and compiler-rt, under the Apache License 2.0 with LLVM
  Exceptions (licenses/libcxx-LICENSE, licenses/libcxxabi-LICENSE,
  licenses/compiler-rt-LICENSE). The binary names no compiler. The Dockerfile
  names the image emscripten/emsdk:3.1.74, and the five texts are that
  version's. musl's messages and the type names of libc++ and libc++abi are
  in the binary. That compiler-rt is in it too, and dlmalloc, Emscripten's
  default allocator, which is in the public domain, follows from how
  Emscripten builds and was not read from the binary.
